Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS  
  – "sample_path": locate files that end with “.swift”.  
  – "binary": filter out binary files (keep “FALSE”).  
  – "copies": number of repositories that contain an identical file‑hash; the larger the value, the more “copied” the file is.  
  – "id": unique identifier of every file blob.  
  – "sample_repo_name": repository that holds the file content.  

• (No other table is strictly required for the core task, but joins can be demonstrated)  

Typical conditions that will be useful  
WHERE "binary" = FALSE  
AND   "sample_path" ILIKE '%.swift'  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (each limited to 20 rows) that progress from simple inspection toward the final answer.  
All identifiers are wrapped in double quotes as requested.

```sql
--Description: 1) Peek at a handful of Swift files (any binary state).
SELECT "id",
       "sample_repo_name",
       "sample_path",
       "binary",
       "copies"
FROM   "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_CONTENTS"
WHERE  "sample_path" ILIKE '%.swift'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) Show distinct repositories that contain at least one Swift file.
SELECT DISTINCT "sample_repo_name"
FROM   "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_CONTENTS"
WHERE  "sample_path" ILIKE '%.swift'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) Swift files that are explicitly non‑binary.
SELECT "id",
       "sample_repo_name",
       "sample_path",
       "copies"
FROM   "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_CONTENTS"
WHERE  "binary" = FALSE
  AND  "sample_path" ILIKE '%.swift'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Top 20 most copied non‑binary Swift files (raw order by "copies").
SELECT "id",
       "sample_repo_name",
       "sample_path",
       "copies"
FROM   "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_CONTENTS"
WHERE  "binary" = FALSE
  AND  "sample_path" ILIKE '%.swift'
ORDER  BY "copies" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) Use a window function to rank non‑binary Swift files by copy count.
SELECT "id",
       "sample_repo_name",
       "sample_path",
       "copies",
       RANK() OVER(ORDER BY "copies" DESC) AS "swift_copy_rank"
FROM   "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_CONTENTS"
WHERE  "binary" = FALSE
  AND  "sample_path" ILIKE '%.swift'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Return the maximum copies value among non‑binary Swift files.
SELECT MAX("copies") AS "max_swift_copies"
FROM   "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_CONTENTS"
WHERE  "binary" = FALSE
  AND  "sample_path" ILIKE '%.swift';
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Identify every non‑binary Swift file that matches the maximum copies value.
WITH max_val AS (
  SELECT MAX("copies") AS "mx"
  FROM   "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_CONTENTS"
  WHERE  "binary" = FALSE
    AND  "sample_path" ILIKE '%.swift'
)
SELECT c."id",
       c."sample_repo_name",
       c."sample_path",
       c."copies"
FROM   "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_CONTENTS" c,
       max_val
WHERE  c."binary" = FALSE
  AND  c."sample_path" ILIKE '%.swift'
  AND  c."copies" = max_val."mx"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Same as query 7 but bring in license information (if available) for those repos.
WITH max_val AS (
  SELECT MAX("copies") AS "mx"
  FROM   "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_CONTENTS"
  WHERE  "binary" = FALSE
    AND  "sample_path" ILIKE '%.swift'
)
SELECT c."id",
       c."sample_repo_name",
       l."license",
       c."sample_path",
       c."copies"
FROM   "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_CONTENTS" c
LEFT  JOIN "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LICENSES" l
       ON c."sample_repo_name" = l."repo_name",
       max_val
WHERE  c."binary" = FALSE
  AND  c."sample_path" ILIKE '%.swift'
  AND  c."copies" = max_val."mx"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) Demonstrate a tighter search by also requiring copies ≥ 5 (arbitrary threshold).
SELECT "id",
       "sample_repo_name",
       "sample_path",
       "copies"
FROM   "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_CONTENTS"
WHERE  "binary" = FALSE
  AND  "sample_path" ILIKE '%.swift'
  AND  "copies" >= 5
ORDER  BY "copies" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 10) FINAL ANSWER QUERY – return the repository (or repositories, in case of a tie) that contains the single most‑copied non‑binary Swift file, each file uniquely identified by its ID.
WITH ranked_swift AS (
  SELECT "id",
         "sample_repo_name",
         "copies",
         RANK() OVER(ORDER BY "copies" DESC) AS "rnk"
  FROM   "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_CONTENTS"
  WHERE  "binary" = FALSE
    AND  "sample_path" ILIKE '%.swift'
)
SELECT "id"                AS "file_id",
       "sample_repo_name"  AS "repository_name",
       "copies"            AS "copy_count"
FROM   ranked_swift
WHERE  "rnk" = 1
LIMIT 20;
```
